                    insight_reinvented: `Reinvented and funded: value proposition, monetization and operations describe one coherent company, the board and lead investor approve the pivot, and you reached it inside the €1.8M runway. You diagnosed the structural failure and redesigned the model rather than inheriting its flaws — Dauchy's coherence test passed end to end.`,
                    insight_approved: `The board approves the pivot: the model holds together well enough to back, off the declining print P&L. It is credible, if not yet exceptional — tighten the coherence and confidence further and this is a model that compounds.`,
                    insight_insolvent: `You died solvent-on-paper: the model may have been attractive, but the cash ran out before break-even. A reinvention under a cash clock must pass the coherence test within the runway you actually have — the cash-flow shape, not just the total, is what kills you.`,
                    insight_blocked: `The board blocks the plan and moves toward a sale. Either the components contradicted each other or you never won the investor's confidence — most likely a digital promise bolted onto a print P&L without a real change in operating logic.`,
                    insight_incoherent: `Coherence stayed low — your value proposition, revenue model and operations describe different companies. A strong business model is defined by the fit between its parts, not by the cleverness of any single element.`,
                    insight_lowconfidence: `Investor confidence never reached the ≥70 needed to approve a pivot. The lead seed investor backs a coherent reinvention, not digital bolted onto a print P&L — and not a conversion case you couldn't defend.`,
                    insight_thinreserves: `You reach the board with thin reserves: the pivot is funded but the cushion is dangerously small. A subscription compounds slowly — make sure the cash curve clears break-even before the runway is gone.`,
                    insight_funded: `Strong reserves remaining: you reinvented the model and still kept a real cash cushion. That combination — coherence, confidence and runway intact — is what turns a rescue into a durable new business.`,
                    hint_insolvent: `The runway has run out — the model is solvent-on-paper but out of cash. Recurring revenue pays slowly; investment and stranded plant cost must be modelled against the 14-month clock, not just the headline plan.`,
                    hint_cash: `Cash is dangerously low. Recurring revenue compounds slowly — re-check the upfront investment and any stranded plant cost against the €1.8M runway before you reach break-even.`,
                    hint_coherence: `Coherence is weak — your value proposition, revenue model and operations don't yet describe one company. Resolve the contradictions before the pitch; the investor backs fit, not clever fragments.`,
                    hint_confidence: `Investor confidence is low. Anchor the value proposition in the customer's job, size the conversion honestly, and make the operation cohere with the promise — that is what the board is waiting to see.`,
                    hint_strong: `Strong position — coherence and confidence both healthy. Now lock in the operating coherence and an honestly-named risk so the board approves the pivot at the meeting.`,
                    col_step: `Step`,
                    col_move: `Move`,
                    col_coherence: `Coherence`,
                    col_confidence: `Confidence`,
                    col_runway: `Runway`,
                    r1_diag_label: `What is actually failing? State the diagnosis you will defend to the board.`,
                    diag_structural: `The model itself: the proposition is commoditised, the margin is eroding and the cost base is fixed. Three faults, one cause.`,
                    diag_mix: `The mix: we still win the complex work and lose the simple work. Retreat to what we still win.`,
                    diag_demand: `Demand: our clients' budgets moved to channels we do not serve. Follow the budget.`,
                    diag_margin: `Price and cost: we have let the price of print fall faster than the cost of making it.`,
                    r1_asset_label: `Which asset will the reinvention be built on?`,
                    asset_content: `Eight years of design files, brand assets and content for ~600 regional SMEs`,
                    asset_plant: `The plant and the craft — presses, finishing, and people who know how to use them`,
                    asset_brand: `The name: the region's premium house since 2009, and the relationships that came with it`,
                    r1_research_label: `The conversion of the 600 clients decides the whole revenue case. Do you buy the number now?`,
                    research_none: `No research (€0) — back your own reading of the client base`,
                    research_light: `A fast sample of 60 clients (€20k) — indicative, wide error bars`,
                    research_full: `Full segmentation of all 600 (€60k) — you will know the real band before you bet`,
                    r1_research_hint: `You are paying now for a number you will not need until the monetization step — and before you know which model you will choose.`,
                    r2_vp_label: `Commit to one value proposition. Everything you decide after this is judged against it.`,
                    vp_managed: `Managed digital presence — we run the website, social and catalogue for SMEs who cannot`,
                    vp_agencyops: `Production partner to regional agencies — we sell capacity to the agencies, not to their clients`,
                    vp_toolkit: `Self-serve toolkit — templates, brand kits and publishing tools the SME uses without us`,
                    vp_marketplace: `Local-commerce marketplace — put the 600 on one storefront and take a margin on what moves`,
                    vp_premium: `Premium niche print — regulated, luxury and short-run work the commodity houses cannot take`,
                    vp_archive: `License the archive — eight years of assets, licensed back to the clients who commissioned them`,
                    r2_focus_label: `How much of today's business do you keep serving while you build it?`,
                    focus_sharp: `One segment, one job. Exit everything that does not serve it, and say so publicly.`,
                    focus_adjacent: `Keep the adjacent work that funds the build; exit only what actively contradicts the new model.`,
                    focus_broad: `Take every order that comes. Cash today buys time to get the new model right.`,
                    r3_revenue_label: `How does the new model get paid?`,
                    revenue_subscription: `Monthly subscription — a managed service billed per client, compounding`,
